## Phase 3 — Complete

**Test result: 5/5 pass**

### Files written

**`actions/agent/orchestrator_client.py`** — New async HTTP client wrapping all Orchestrator API calls:
- `register_agent(agent_id, role, url)` → `POST /agents/register`
- `report(task_id, step_id, status, ...)` → `POST /tasks/{task_id}/report` (IN_PROGRESS is a no-op log — Orchestrator only accepts COMPLETE/BLOCKED/FAILED)
- `poll_next_task(agent_id)` → `GET /agents/{agent_id}/next-task`
- `update_heartbeat(agent_id)` → `PATCH /agents/{agent_id}/heartbeat`
- Config from env: `ORCHESTRATOR_URL`, `ORCHESTRATOR_API_KEY`, `AGENT_ID`, `AGENT_ROLE`, `AGENT_URL`

**`tests/test_orchestrator_integration.py`** — 5 integration tests (all passing)

### Files modified

**`main.py`** — Added:
- Startup registration via `orchestrator_client.register_agent()` with graceful fallback (no crash if Orchestrator is unreachable)
- `GET /health` endpoint returning `{status, role, uptime_seconds}`
- `POST /task` endpoint: accepts `OrchestratorAssignment`, queues `_run_assigned_task` as a background task, returns 202 immediately

**`services/chat_service.py`** — Fixed the silent chain-break:
- New signature: `chat_with_agent(request, task_id=None, step_id=None)`
- When orchestrated: reports `IN_PROGRESS` → runs → reports `COMPLETE` or `FAILED`
- When `task_id`/`step_id` are `None`: all `report()` calls are skipped (full backward compatibility with legacy `/api/v1/chat` calls)

**`requirements.txt`** — Added `httpx`
